  <p>
    <strong>Digital vehicle inspection software replaces the paper tick sheet with photos and notes a customer can
    see directly</strong>, attached to the specific point on the vehicle they relate to, sent for approval before
    any extra work starts. It's one part of what <a href="/garage-management-software">garage management software</a> covers.
  </p>

  <h2>Why photo inspections change the approval conversation</h2>
  <p>
    A phone call explaining "the rear discs are worn" asks a customer to trust a description. A photo of the actual
    disc, next to the estimate, doesn't. Approval rates and average job value both tend to improve once a customer
    can see what's being described, rather than take it on trust over the phone.
  </p>

  <h2>What a digital inspection covers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Photo evidence attached to each point checked, not just a pass/fail tick.</li>
    <li>Notes and recommendations a customer reads in their own time, not down a phone line.</li>
    <li>Approval captured in the system, so there's a record of what was agreed and when.</li>
    <li>A history attached to the vehicle, so the next inspection can reference the last one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where WhatsApp approvals fit in</h2>
  <p>
    Once an inspection is complete, GarageCloud can send the findings and approval request over WhatsApp — a channel
    most customers already check constantly, rather than a missed call or an email that sits unread until the
    evening. The approved job then shows on the <a href="/features/workshop-board">workshop board</a> like any other.
    See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for which plan includes it.
  </p>
